<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African money shortage rises to eight bln rand.</title>
<headline>S.African money shortage rises to eight bln rand.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's money market shortage edged back up to around eight billion rand at the weekend after dipping last week, the Reserve Bank said on Monday.</p>
<p>The shortage stood at 7.947 billion rand on Saturday from 8.050 billion on Friday and 7.780 billion rand on Thursday.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
